Index: doc/trace.n
==================================================================
--- doc/trace.n
+++ doc/trace.n
@@ -157,10 +157,18 @@
 \fICode\fR gives the result code of that execution, and \fIresult\fR
 the result string.
 \fIOp\fR indicates what operation is being performed on the
 command execution, and is one of \fBleave\fR or \fBleavestep\fR as
 defined above.
+.PP
+Whether \fBleave\fR and \fBleavestep\fR traces are invoked for an
+execution of the command is decided when that execution starts.
+A \fBleave\fR trace added on a command while it is executing (for example,
+by a procedure on itself) is therefore invoked when that execution
+completes only if the command already had execution traces when the
+execution started; otherwise it is first invoked at the end of a later
+execution.
 .PP
 Note that the creation of many \fBenterstep\fR or
 \fBleavestep\fR traces can lead to unintuitive results, since the
 invoked commands from one trace can themselves lead to further
 command invocations for other traces.

